Example: PcieModelOrdered
This example in .bsv and .bs models PCIe producer consumer rules to
model throughput and latency performance. All the run-time parameters
can be passed as environment variables. 
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Build and run instructions:
git clone https://github.com/suhaspai/bsv_and_bs_examples.git
cd bsv_and_bs_examples

# Separately source your bluespec (bsc) environment
source env64.csh   # sets up alised command "chex"
check: alias chex  # to see what it does

chex PcieModelOrdered   # Pick PcieModelOrdered example and cd into it

To create bluesim target (defined in ../bsv.mk)
make synth_bluesim

To run default bluesim target (defined in ../bsv.mk)
make bsim_run  # 10% reads 
make run_sim   # same as above

To do both (defined in ../bsv.mk)
make bluesim

Run write after write  (defined in ./makefile which includes ../bsv.mk)
make waw    # pipelined posted writes, the run is analyzed in analysis.txt
make rar    # pipelined nonposted reads
make raw    # pipelined read after write

The code adheres to all PCIe producer consumering ordering rules (you can prove them! :)
Please let me know if you see any errors.

The classic bluespec version (.bs) is also available which can be compiled using
the following command:

make TARGET=bs synth_bluesim   (the TARGET is set to bsv)

